UPSTREAM WORK
================================================================================

This project contains a modified copy of DezKVM-Go.

    DezKVM-Go
    Copyright (C) tobychui
    https://github.com/tobychui/DezKVM-Go
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0

The entire web front-end, together with the Go HTTPS helper in src/,
originates there. That includes the paste box, the OCR copy box,
the on-screen keyboard, quick-access hotkeys and macros, the screen recorder,
stacked keys, the mouse jiggler, the settings panel, and the CH9329 byte
serialisation that this project's firmware was written to match.


================================================================================
MODIFICATIONS (GPLv3 section 5a)
================================================================================

Modified by Ben Meadors on 2026-08-15.

Fork point: tobychui/DezKVM-Go commit 7195239e557747784d0da68eb2be6d2cc6bb4e9b
(2026-08-07). Changes relative to that commit:

Added
  firmware/                   ESP32-S3 firmware (ESP-IDF + TinyUSB). Presents a
                              boot-protocol HID keyboard and an absolute mouse to
                              the target, and accepts CH9329-compatible frames
                              from the host on UART0 at 115200. New work, GPLv3.
                              Deviates from byte-faithful CH9329 emulation in two
                              documented places; see docs/PROTOCOL.md section 7.
  tools/ch9329_test.py        Protocol test harness. New work, GPLv3.
  tools/verify_descriptors.py USB descriptor validator. New work, GPLv3.
  docs/PROTOCOL.md            The CH9329 wire protocol as the UI actually speaks
                              it, extracted from local-kvm.js. New work.
  NOTICE                      This file.

Rewritten as a Nuxt/Vue application
  The web front-end was rebuilt as a Nuxt 4 + Vue 3 + TypeScript app under web/,
  replacing the inherited jQuery/DOM-driven implementation. It is styled with
  Tailwind CSS and statically generated. The Fomantic-UI CDN dependency was
  dropped -- it made an on-site tool require an internet connection -- along with
  jQuery, main.css and the upstream logo.

  The behaviour of upstream's features was ported rather than reinvented: the
  paste box, OCR copy box, on-screen keyboard, quick-access hotkeys, screen
  recorder, stacked keys, mouse jiggler and settings all originate from
  DezKVM-Go. web/app/utils/ch9329.ts is a faithful port of upstream's CH9329 byte
  serialisation, including its quirks (JS keycode 18 maps to Right Alt; modifier
  usages travel in the keycode array), and web/test/ asserts the same golden
  frames the Python harness and the firmware were verified against.

  Tesseract is now vendored in web/public/vendor/tesseract (engine, worker, WASM
  core and English training data) so OCR works with no network. The other OCR
  languages still fetch their training data at runtime and are marked as such.

  Deployment moved to GitHub Actions (.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml), which
  builds the site and publishes it to Pages. src/sync_www.sh builds a
  root-relative copy for the Go server to embed.

Changed (applied to the inherited files before the rewrite above superseded them)
  local-kvm.js                Added the MS2130 capture dongle (534d:2130,
                              345f:2130) to supportedVidPidPairs, ahead of the
                              existing MS2109 entries which are retained. Added a
                              1080p60 entry to MODE_LIST for the MS2130. Reworded
                              two MS2109-specific console/toast messages to refer
                              to the capture device generically.

  settings.html               Reworded the HID Baudrate field description: this
                              firmware always starts at 115200, so the CH9329
                              9600-baud reconfiguration step does not apply. The
                              9600 option itself is retained for use with real
                              CH9329 hardware. Updated the About tab's supported
                              hardware list from MS2109 + CH9329 to MS2130 +
                              ESP32-S3, noting both older parts still work.

  README.md                   Rewritten for this hardware and setup flow.

Removed
  PCB/                        Not copied. See below.
  3D Models/
  img/                        Upstream branding, replaced by this fork's own UI.


================================================================================
HARDWARE ASSETS DELIBERATELY NOT INCLUDED
================================================================================

Upstream licenses its hardware assets -- the PCB/ and "3D Models/" directories --
under Creative Commons BY-NC-ND (Attribution, NonCommercial, NoDerivatives).
NoDerivatives means they may not be modified and redistributed, so they are not
copied into this repository in any form, modified or otherwise.

This project does not need them: it uses a stock ESP32-S3 dev board and an
off-the-shelf HDMI capture dongle. Obtain the reference hardware from upstream
under its own terms.


================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
================================================================================

Tesseract.js 5 and tesseract.js-core (Apache-2.0), with Tesseract English
training data (Apache-2.0), vendored in web/public/vendor/tesseract/ so optical
character recognition works without a network connection.

Nuxt, Vue and Tailwind CSS (all MIT) are build-time dependencies pulled by npm;
they are not vendored into this repository.

Upstream's Fomantic-UI and jQuery dependencies were removed in this rewrite.

The firmware pulls espressif/esp_tinyusb and espressif/tinyusb at build time via
the ESP-IDF component manager; both are Apache-2.0 / MIT and are not vendored
into this repository.
